-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",260,{
[8289]="700304CC\n1\tFind out why Etta suddenly protests\tEtta, mother of Thane Radwig, is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend. You should speak with Etta.\n2\tHear Radwig's reply\tThe young Thane Radwig is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend. You should speak with Radwig.\n3\tTalk to Radwig at Nîn-stazg\tRadwig wishes to meet you outside of Nîn-stazg, an Orc-encampment in the south-east of the Wold. You should search for Radwig near Nîn-stazg, for he wishes to help you drive out the Orcs there.\n4\tDestroy siege-machines (total: 3)\tSiege machines can be found at Nîn-stazg to the south-east of Floodwend. You should destroy siege-weapons that you find in the woods.\n5\tReturn to Radwig outside of Nîn-stazg\tThane Radwig is on a hill overlooking Nîn-stazg. You should speak with Thane Radwig.\n",
[8290]="700442B6\n1\tRetrieve abandoned weapons (total: 6)\030Retrieve abandoned shields (total: 6)\tMen cast aside their weapons and shields when they fled in terror from their posts along the wall at the north end of the Third Circle. Ingold has asked you to retrieve the weapons and shields the men dropped when they fled. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n2\tTalk to Ingold in the besieged city, atop the wall at the north end of the Third Circle\tIngold is the besieged city, atop the wall at the north end of the Third Circle. You have retrieved weapons and shields cast aside by men when they fled, and should return now to Ingold. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n3\tFrightened soldiers can be found in the besieged city, at the north end of the Third Circle. Ingold has asked you to convince the men that ran from their posts to return. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\t\n4\tTalk to Ingold in the besieged city, atop the wall at the north end of the Third Circle\tIngold is in the besieged city, atop the wall at the north end of the Third Circle. You have convinced some of the fleeing men to return to their posts, despite their terror. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n",
[8291]="70042F56\n1\tImprisoned Rangers can be found in and around Meneldil's Square in western Osgiliath. Halhir has asked you to free imprisoned Rangers of Ithilien before they are executed in Meneldil's Square.\t\n2\tTalk to Halhir\tHalhir can be found due east of the Palace of Eldacar in western Osgiliath. You have rescued many imprisoned Rangers and should now return to Halhir.\n",
[8292]="7002EE5D\n1\tDefeat salamanders and crebain in the Wódfen (total: 10)\tSalamanders and crebain can be found in the Wódfen. You should defeat many salamanders and crebain to see if you can discover the source of their madness.\n",
[8293]="7003FFEE\n1\tSearch for the source of the spiders' madness in Lhingroth\tThe cave of Lhingroth can be found in the hills to the east of Sardol. Amathon has asked you to brave the depths of Lhingroth in hopes of finding what has roused the spiders.\n2\tSearch for the source of the chill in Lhingroth\tThe chill seems to be emanating from the path to the right in Lhingroth. You feel a peculiar chill inside Lhingroth and should investigate further.\n3\tExamine the skeleton beneath the altar in Lhingroth\tA suspiciously preserved skeleton can be found in the depths of Lhingroth. You have found a strange altar, and what appear to be preserved bones. You should examine them before returning to Amathon.\n4\tTalk to Amathon\tAmathon can be found in Sardol, to the west of Lhingroth. You have been confronted by an oath-breaker of the Ruthless Dead who warned of their intent to break their curse without fulfilling it.\n",
[8294]="700733C2\n1\tVisit the entrance to the neighbourhood\030Visit the dell commons\030Visit a Simple Cottage\030Visit a Villa\030Visit a Grand Villa\030Find a good view of the Valley\030Find a view of the Trollshaws\tThe entrance to homestead glens of Imladris can be found south of the stables of Rivendell. Hirthamel has suggested you explore the hills and hollows, and perhaps consider residing there yourself.\n2\tReturn to Hirthamel\tYou should return to Hirthamel to share what you have seen\n",
[8295]="70054659\n1\tDestroy blood orbs (total: 8)\tBlood orbs can be found in Kaslokroz, an Uruk-hai camp. You should destroy the blood orbs.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tYou have destroyed the blood orbs in Rûkhor's camp. You should report your success to Legolas near Kaslokroz.\n",
[8296]="7006BE9A\n1\tDefeat Urâshi sandstorms (total: 4)\030Defeat Urâshi wasps (total: 8)\tShukûri has asked you to thin the numbers of wasps and sandstorms within the Gorge of Woe.\n2\tReturn to Shukûri\tReturn to Shukûri in the Gorge of Woe and let her know that you have thinned the number of enemies in the area.\n",
[8297]="70043DFE\n1\tDestroy enemy food sacks (total: 10)\tEnemy food sacks can be found on the Western side of Osgiliath. You should destroy enemy food sacks.\n2\tListen to Grazadhal yell at you\tGrazadhal is at Dâr Dugoth. You should speak to Grazadhal.\n",
[8298]="70066585\n1\tCollect dry driftwood (total: 8)\tNarthrien suggests you collect driftwood that is dry enough to be salvageable.\n2\tTalk to Narthrien in Parth Rest\tYou have collected a healthy amount of driftwood that could be of use as lumber in Parth Rest. You should bring it back to Narthrien. Narthrien can be found in Parth Rest.\n",
[8299]="7002FE1D\n1\tBehead Orcs (total: 12)\tFastred wants you to gather Orc heads to add to the grim display outside Snowbourn. Orcs can be found throughout the Sutcrofts.\n2\tTalk to Fastred in Snowbourn's mead-hall\tFastred will be pleased to hear that you have added to the collection of Orc heads outside Snowbourn. Fastred can be found inside the mead-hall in Snowbourn.\n",
[8300]="7002EDFA\n1\tCollect sacks of flour (total: 5)\030Collect sacks of vegetables (total: 5)\030Collect slabs of aurochs-meat (total: 5)\tSacks of flour and vegetables can be found within the Eaworth Vendor Hall. Offram wants you to collect sacks of flour and vegetables to finish making meat-pies for the inhabitants of Eaworth.\n2\tTake meat, flour, and vegetables to Ordbéorth's oven and bake meat-pies\tOrdbéorth's oven can be found behind his house in the northern part of Eaworth. Offram wants you to take the meat, flour, and vegetables to Ordbéorth's oven and bake meat-pies for the inhabitants of Eaworth.\n3\tPeople in need of provisions can be found throughout Eaworth. Offram wants you to take the meat-pies you baked to people in need of provisions for the siege.\t\n4\tTalk to Offram outside the Vendor Hall in Eaworth\tOffram stands guard outside the Vendor Hall in Eaworth. You should return to Offram and let him know that you have delivered the meat-pies.\n",
[8301]="70025081\n1\tFind a good place to set off the fireworks\tThe fireworks are stored at the top of the stairs overlooking the Festival Square. You should set off the fireworks to distract the wealthy patrons of the Festival.\n2\tMany wealthy patrons have been distracted by your mischief! You should pick the pockets of the wealthy patrons for coins to give to the poor.\t\n3\tReturn to Gareth Rust with the pilfered coins\tGareth Rust is in the workers' area in Winter-home. You should return to Gareth Rust and find out if he saw your excellent firework display.\n",
[8302]="7006B60B\n1\tPick up a pile of papyrus reeds\tCollect reeds from the pile across the yard at Mehêtur, and bring them to the workbench.\n2\tUse the workbench to prepare the reeds\tYou have a pile of papyrus reeds. Take them to the workbench, remove the green skin, and cut them into strips.\n3\tUse the workbench to weave the strips together\tYou have peeled the papyrus and cut the inside of the reeds into thin strips. Now you should weave them together at the workbench.\n4\tUse the workbench to press the woven reeds under a weight\tYou have woven the papyrus strips together. The next step is to press them under a heavy weight.\n5\tTalk to Sûlmur\tYou have completed all the steps of making papyrus. You should talk to Sûlmur.\n",
[8303]="70037785\n1\tCollect spears and shields (total: 3)\030Collect saddles (total: 6)\tShields, spears, and saddles can be found throughout the refugees' small camp north of Marton. You should collect spears, shields, and saddles for the journey, and ready the horses.\n2\tSaddle the horses (total: 6)\tThe refugees' horses can be found at the head of their camp, north of Marton. You should saddle the horses to ready them for the dangerous journey to Helm's Deep.\n3\tSpeak with Agelwyn\tAgelwyn is in the refugees' small camp in the ravine north of Marton. You should speak with Agelwyn.\n",
[8304]="700430A3\n1\tTalk to Hathalon on the height, north-west of the Hall of Lady Vanyalos\tHathalon can be found at the sparring area high up in Imloth Melui, north-west of the Hall of Lady Vanyalos. Captain Merenir has asked you to help Hathalon train some of the new recruits.\n2\tTalk to a young recruit at the sparring area in Imloth Melui\tThe sparring area is high up in Imloth Melui, west of Lady Vanyalos' quarters. Fresh recruits are ready to spar with you in an effort to improve their skills.\n3\tTalk to another young recruit at the sparring area in Imloth Melui\tThe sparring area is high up in Imloth Melui, west of Lady Vanyalos' quarters. Fresh recruits are ready to spar with you in an effort to improve their skills.\n4\tTalk to one more young recruit at the sparring area in Imloth Melui\tThe sparring area is high up in Imloth Melui, west of Lady Vanyalos' quarters. Fresh recruits are ready to spar with you in an effort to improve their skills.\n5\tTalk to Hathalon on the height, north-west of the Hall of Lady Vanyalos\tHathalon can be found at the sparring area high up in Imloth Melui, west of the Hall of Lady Vanyalos. You helped Hathalon train some of the new recruits, and should see what he thought of your lessons.\n",
[8305]="70020DBD\n1\tCollect stag-antlers (total: 10)\tWhite stags can be found throughout the Gloomglens in Enedwaith. Rhosun Turio has asked you to collect stag-antlers for her to continue her scrimshaw.\n2\tTalk to Rhosun Turio at Maur Tulhau\tRhosun Turio can be found in Maur Tulhau in the Gloomglens of Enedwaith. You should bring the stag-antlers you collected back to Rhosun Turio.\n",
[8306]="7006C8DE\n1\tBring the ingot to Dashên in Iridír\tTibira has asked you to take her copper ingot to Dashên at Iridír in Ambarûl and trade it for fresh produce.\n2\tTalk to Dashên\tTibira has asked you to take her copper ingot to Dashên at Iridír in Ambarûl and trade it for fresh produce. You should talk to Dashên.\n3\tBring the provisions to Tibira in Western Khanâg\tYou have traded Tibira's copper ingot to Dashên at Iridír in Ambarûl for fresh produce. You should return to Tibira at Western Khanâg in Khûd Zagin with the crate.\n",
[8307]="700032F7\n1\tCollect eggs (total: 4)\tThe chicken nests are around Farmer Sandson's yard. Farmer Sandson has asked you to gather some eggs from his chicken nests, but warned you to stay away from the rooster. If he sees you while you are gathering the eggs, they will call out and upset the other chickens. Furthermore, you are sure to drop the eggs you've collected! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tBring the eggs to Farmer Sandson\tFarmer Sandson is at his farm, west of Waymeet. You managed to gather enough eggs without being noticed by the rooster. You should take them back to Farmer Sandson.\n",
[8308]="70066EEA\n1\tLeave Tadrent by the northern entrance and circle around the town to the left\tOsbenn asked you to leave Tadrent by the northern entrance and circle the town to the left.\n2\tContinue circling the town of Tadrent for Guard Osbenn\tYou have have begun making Osbenn's rounds for him, and should continue to circle the town of Tadrent on his behalf.\n3\tContinue circling the town of Tadrent for Guard Osbenn\tYou have reached the halfway point of Osbenn's rounds, and should continue to circle the town of Tadrent on his behalf.\n4\tWhile making his rounds for Guard Osbenn, you have found the corpse of a Corsair.\t\n5\tTalk to Guard Osbenn in Tadrent, King's Gondor\tGuard Osbenn is in the centre of Tadrent, in King's Gondor.\n",
[8309]="70018F57\n1\tExamine Malbrethil-saplings (total: 4)\tMalbrethil-saplings can be found in Taur Hith, north-east of Cerin Amroth. Mallendathor would like you to find and examine some Malbrethil-saplings.\n2\tTalk to Mallendathor at Cerin Amroth\tMallendathor is near Cerin Amroth, south-west of Taur Hith. You should tell Mallendathor about the Malbrethil-saplings you found.\n",
[8310]="7006DFB1\n1\tDeliver the gorgeous dust to a collection box\030Collect gorgeous dust ([see journal]/10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire gorgeous dust.\n",
[8311]="7006DFB2\n1\tDeliver the tapered carapaces to a collection box\030Collect tapered carapaces ([see journal]/10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire tapered carapaces.\n",
[8312]="7006DFB4\n1\tDeliver the vile essences to a collection box\030Collect vile essences ([see journal]/10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire vile essences.\n",
[8313]="7006DFB0\n1\tDeliver the vile filth to a collection box\030Collect vile filth ([see journal]/10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire vile filth.\n",
[8314]="7006DFB3\n1\tDeliver the vile finger bones to a collection box\030Collect vile finger bones ([see journal]/10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire vile finger bones.\n",
[8315]="7005465A\n1\tDefeat Ungoladan devoted (total: 3)\tLegolas has asked you to defeat Ungoladan devoted in Cadar Skûs.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tYou have defeated the highest ranking Ungoledain at Cadar Skûs. You should talk to Legolas.\n",
[8316]="70035994\n1\tTalk to Mossbeard\tMossbeard can be found at Stonecliff in the Balewood. Mossbeard is prepared to tell you and the Ents of the rest of what he has learned from the trees of the forest. You should listen to his tale when you are ready.\n2\tTalk to Mossbeard\tMossbeard can be found at Stonecliff in the Balewood. Mossbeard's tale of Saruman and Núrzum has concluded. You should now speak with him of what can be done to stop the forces at work in the Balewood.\n",
[8317]="70000C34\n1\tDefeat angered Tarkrîps (total: 12)\030Defeat dreadful Tarkrîps (total: 10)\tThe Orcs can be found in the ruins of Ost Cyrn, south-west of Ost Guruth. Grimdeal asked that you help defend the Eglain by assaulting the Orcs of Ost Cyrn.\n2\tTalk to Grimdeal\tGrimdeal awaits word of your success at Ost Guruth, north-east of Ost Cyrn. You should return to Grimdeal with word of your victory.\n",
[8318]="70067C3F\n1\tYou must head south along the road and then make your way west toward the Haradrim encampment of Grijâti to search for the captives taken from the attack on the caravan. Rescue the eight travellers and return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl.\t\n2\tReturn to Girgish at Jax Phanâl\tYou successfully rescued eight of the caravan captives. Return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl and tell her of your success.\n",
[8319]="70060715\n1\tFind Mandan by one of the rivers north-east of Tornhad\tMandan often walks far and wide throughout the Angle, but Mithrendan thinks you should look for the Herb-master somewhere by a river north-east of Tornhad.\n2\tTalk to Mandan\tYou found Mandan on an island in the middle of a river north-east of Tornhad, and the herb-master of the Dúnedain seems to be in no more danger than that to which he is accustomed.\n3\tCollect luminescent gel from glow-flies (total: 6)\030Collect damp mushrooms, even though Mandan doesn't want them (total: 3)\030Collect sharp reeds from the river-bank (total: 5)\tThe Ranger Mandan has asked for your help gathering a number of the items for which he left Tornhad: luminescent gel from the glow-flies of the Angle, damp mushroom caps, and sharp reeds from the nearby river-bank.\n4\tBring the items you gathered to Mandan\tMandan is on the island in the middle of a river north-east of Tornhad, waiting for you to return with the items he requested.\n5\tTalk to Mithrendan in Tornhad\tThe Ranger Mithrendan is at Tornhad.\n",
[8320]="7002ADD4\n1\tHelp as many customers as you can during your shift\tCustomers of the Farmers Market are lining up at the vendor stall. You should help fill as many orders as you can before your shift is over.\n",
})
